jabraw (0.4.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Change a setting from the dialog, where the values are established: pick a
    row, pick a value, and the daemon writes it over whichever transport is
    there and reports what the device answered. Settings whose value shares a
    byte with its neighbours are refused rather than guessed at.

 -- Michael Dold <michidold@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0200

jabraw (0.4.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read the settings that address a sub-item through a payload byte, carry
    their value at an index other than the first, or occupy only part of a
    byte. Five more settings show their value by name: ringtone volume,
    ringtone, boom arm rotation, button function and the DSP sidetone level.

 -- Michael Dold <michidold@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:47:00 +0200

jabraw (0.4.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show the values of seven settings under their names instead of a number —
    auto sleep 12 reads as two hours, voice prompts 2 as off. The byte for each
    value comes from jabridge under Apache-2.0; see doc/settings-sources.md and
    debian/copyright.

 -- Michael Dold <michidold@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:12:00 +0200

jabraw (0.4.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reconnect over Bluetooth. BlueZ answers ConnectProfile with success while
    it still counts the profile as connected, and hands over no socket, so
    every attempt after the first sat out its timeout. The profile is torn
    down first now.
  * Start the daemon when a headset connects over Bluetooth, through the input
    device bluetoothd creates for its AVRCP keys. Only the dongle triggered
    that before.

 -- Michael Dold <michidold@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:05:00 +0200

